cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite HINC-001 as a public-review candidate package. Cite a later DOI or
  archival release if one becomes available.
title: Hidden Infinitesimal Noncommutativity in Endomorphism Monoids of Two Graded Gerstenhaber Algebras
type: article
version: 0.1.0-public-review
date-released: 2026-07-27
authors:
  - family-names: Novak
    given-names: Matthew S.
abstract: >-
  We give a self-contained candidate classification of graded binary-Gerstenhaber
  endomorphism monoid schemes for two explicit characteristic-two subalgebras of
  the Hochschild cohomology of the dual numbers. The two monoids share a reduced
  crossing core but differ by a constrained infinitesimal skew thickening and a
  separate clopen torus unit component. A bounded algebraic kernel and the
  principal coefficient classifications are publicly proof-assistant verified;
  the complete scheme-level manuscript remains under specialist and
  historical-equivalence review. One or more large language models materially
  assisted the research under human direction; specific model and provider
  identities are not disclosed in this release.
repository-code: https://github.com/novakprotocol/N-Human-AI-Mathematics
keywords:
  - algebraic monoids
  - Gerstenhaber algebra
  - Hochschild cohomology
  - nonreduced schemes
  - formal verification
  - human-AI mathematics
  - LLM-assisted research
